==Strategy==
Like others Sequential Advent Stages, this stage is exact copied of [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|N-1 Grand Prix]] and its continuation stage is exact copied of [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]], reading strategies from both stages would also be helpful when building a lineup.

Since the continuation stage demanded fast units, most Normal Cats wouldn't be helpful much in continuation stage due to theirs sluggish speed. Thankfully, because rarity restrictions only applied to Wahwah stage, you can add units such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion]], etc to your lineup. Although unusable against Wahwah, they are helpful for continuation stage.

For continuation stage, it is recommended to add units from Plan B strategy (see [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]] strategy) and perform Plan B in continuation stage.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]]: Although not very helpful in continuation stage, they are still recommended due to being few usable meatshields in Wahwah stage.
*[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]: A tanker that can also deal chip damage against Wahwah and his peons. Still not really helpful in continuation stage.
''Note: these units below aren't usable in Wahwah stage but are still helpful in Clionel stage enough making them worth bringing''
*[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]]: Acts as a meatshield and a rusher. His main usage is stopping Clionel from moving and clearing Trolly Blogger.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: The key in No Plan A, if done correctly, he can put Clionel back to underworld.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Being spammable while having ridiculously high defense against Angel, he is primary meatshield in continuation stage.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]: In his normal form, he can deal great damage against both bosses and he is spammable enough to be use as additional meatshield on Wahwah stage. If you happen to have his Ultra Form, say goodbye to yours brain then you can mindlessly spam him to win both stage.
*Any Rusher Ubers are helpful such as [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]] who can do wonder in both stages if given opportunity to hit Wahwah or entered Clionel blindspot.
*[[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Ushiwakamaru]]: In his normal form he is spammable enough to be use as additional meatshield and can do chip damage on Wahwah stage. However, the main reason he is recommended is because he can solo continuation stage.

==Trivia==
*Since [[King Wahwah]]'s Japanese description reveals him to be part of a ''[[wikipedia:Manzai|manzai]]'' comedy duo with [[Mistress Celeboodle]], N-1 Grand Prix is likely named after the [[wikipedia:M-1 Grand Prix|M-1 Grand Prix]], the most prevalent ''manzai'' competition in Japan. The "N" presumably stands for ''nyan'', meaning "meow", while the "1" sounds like ''wan'', meaning "woof".
**It is also possible—albeit less likely—that N-1 Grand Prix is a reference to the [[wikia:megaman:N1 Grand Prix|N1 Grand Prix]] in the ''MegaMan Battle Network'' series. In both the games and anime, this is a battle tournament between powerful Navis and Operators

